                        "target_lang_word": "loitering munition",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loitering munition",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9028dcfb-ede5-3487-82ac-bcf479c58451",
                                        "entry_id": "96f421f8-ca29-38bf-be1b-de8bd93f5bce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A munition, often a UAV, that waits passively around the target area and attacks only once a target is located."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11b81584-36ee-4608-b290-785acef4644f",
                                                "sense_id": "9028dcfb-ede5-3487-82ac-bcf479c58451",
                                                "text": "Loitering munitions can circle overhead for extended periods of time, searching for potential targets over a wide area and, once they find one, destroy it. Unlike homing munitions, loitering munitions do not require precise intelligence on enemy targets before launch."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00c15886-790b-493b-bf5f-873a4c3bdd4b",
                                                "sense_id": "9028dcfb-ede5-3487-82ac-bcf479c58451",
                                                "text": "She noted that the report stated the Kargu-2 and “other loitering munitions” attacked convoys and retreating fighters. Loitering munitions, which are simpler autonomous weapons that are designed to hover on their own in an area before crashing into a target, have been used in several other conflicts, Ms. Franke said."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
